  "releaseNotes": "Kazo OS 3.2.0, changes for app developers:\n- The server issues the real-network grant approved in the OS, with its ports. Once an administrator approves network.real.access, the OS asks the connected server to issue the grant (POST /api/proxy/grants) with the approved ports, kept in the new [real-network-ports] section of /etc/kazoos/app-permissions.config, and checks it again at each sync. An app update that declares a new port asks for approval again. The operator can refuse these grants with KazoOs:Proxy:AcceptOsGrants = false.\nRelease notes: https://github.com/Kazo-ca/Os/releases/tag/v3.2.0",
